    LLM: 'Game: German Whist. Set trump by initial upcard, play 13 stock-replenished tricks then 13 closed tricks; standard winner is majority of second-stage tricks.',
    Player: 'German Whist: treat stage one as card drafting, then convert that edge in the final 13 scoring tricks.',
    objective: 'Win the majority of the 13 tricks in stage two after stock is exhausted.',
    gameplay: 'Non-dealer leads first trick. For each trick, second player follows suit if possible in standard form. Higher card of led suit wins unless a trump is played to a non-trump lead. In stage one, trick winner takes the exposed stock card and trick loser takes next hidden stock card; winner then leads next trick. After 13 tricks, stock is empty and stage two begins with no replenishment. Play 13 final tricks; these determine winner in standard scoring.',
